    description: "Twig template names are not looked up as files of the tree: an in-tree template stays a module stand-in.\n\nRepro: synth/tpl/page.twig with {%% extends 'base.twig' %%} and tpl/base.twig present -> dst twig:base.twig:0-0:module:module (not the file node). Twig resolves templates through loader paths the source does not state, so a lookup needs a rule (same directory, then templates/ roots?).\n\nCLOSE WHEN an in-tree template the include names ends on its file node, with the rule stated.\n\nFound by the PR 3 (stable-id v16) WI-tatop build, 2026-11-19; evidence ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/tatop/RESULTS.md (Residuals)."  # 3e87
